  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying  L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{x}+4x+3}{2x+3} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[\\sqrt{x}+4x+3]^{\u2032}}{[2x+3]^{\u2032}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+4}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
